{
 "rule": "upstream's own evaluator, run over generated case sets; held to this repository's scorer by packages/core/test/rcaeval-evaluator.test.ts",
 "note": "Every verdict below was computed by RCAEval's `Evaluator`, not by a transcription of it. A case is `[answer, ...ranking]` as indexes into `services`; `accuracy` is AC@1..AC@5 and `average5` is upstream's `average(5)`, both unrounded so the assertion can round once. Selection: the 17 `design` sets separate the readings a transcription can conflate (rank positions inside and beyond max_k, a ranking that omits the answer, a repeated candidate, denominators whose per-k rates are not representable in two decimals); the 29 `disagreed` sets are the ones that came out 0.01 away before this record existed, when the scorer averaged per-k rates that had already been rounded; the 40 `control` sets agreed then and are kept so the record can still notice a divergence somewhere else. The search that found them covered 317 sets and 6162 cases.",
 "provenance": {
  "repo": "phamquiluan/RCAEval",
  "branch": "main",
  "commit": "259ea4167160256a74ad30004aa3d96a998c846e",
  "committedAt": "2026-09-29T13:30:32Z",
  "readAt": "2026-10-17",
  "maxK": 5,
  "files": [
   {"path": "RCAEval/benchmark/evaluation.py", "sha256": "0a9fadf6d2d58a53ae26dfa66bf680802dbfc20b82b1817989b49413cc1d2502"},
