  ],
  "howToReproduce": [
   "GET https://api.github.com/repos/phamquiluan/RCAEval/contents/<path>?ref=<commit> for each file above and check its sha256",
   "lay them out as RCAEval/benchmark/evaluation.py and RCAEval/classes/graph.py beside empty RCAEval/__init__.py, RCAEval/classes/__init__.py and RCAEval/benchmark/__init__.py",
   "add RCAEval/graph_heads/__init__.py from the same commit, which classes/graph.py imports",
   "add RCAEval/utility.py defining dump_json and load_json, which evaluation.py imports and never calls while the real utility package pulls pandas, sklearn, requests and tqdm",
   "for each set: Evaluator(max_k=5), then add_case(ranks=[Node(services[r], 'unknown') for r in ranking], answer=Node(services[answer], 'unknown'))",
   "record accuracy(1..5) and average(5) unrounded"
  ],
  "whyThisCommit": "The metric's `source` field cited cruiseresearchgroup/RCAEval, whose default branch is v2, whose last push was 2026-02-17, and which has no `main`; the repository the corpus registry points at, and the one whose README publishes the Avg@5 numbers this metric claims to reproduce, is phamquiluan/RCAEval. The two copies compute the same arithmetic, checked by reading both, so the quantity was never in doubt -- only the citation was."
 },
